WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:37.366
Hi everyone,

00:00:37.366 --> 00:00:40.100
I'm Hiker CP. I'm here again,
ready to go hiking abroad.

00:00:42.466 --> 00:00:44.500
An ambulance?? This is my
second time in Malaysia.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:46.700
It’s been nearly 15 years
since I was last here.

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:50.833
It’s very similar to my last trip to Indonesia—and once again,
I’m here hiking with Celine.

00:00:50.833 --> 00:00:53.066
This time, we're going to climb a real
mountain called Shen Mountain.

00:00:53.066 --> 00:00:55.766
As for the route this time,
it won't just be Shen Mountain—

00:00:55.766 --> 00:00:58.666
A two
-day, one-night trip—it’s that simple. This time, we’re going to hike the Sacred Mountain Range.

00:00:58.666 --> 00:01:02.133
In addition to being Southeast Asia's highest peak at 4,
000 meters, Mount Shen...

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:05.433
It's taller than Yushan, and there are three more peaks behind it,
so there are four in total.

00:01:05.433 --> 00:01:08.433
So this time, we're going to hike up to this range of peaks,
which just opened this year.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.866
Oh, it's not just staying at the mountain cabin—we
stayed there on the first day and the second day.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.966
On the third day, we'll be staying at a very high altitude.
How high?

00:01:13.966 --> 00:01:14.666
It's really high.

00:01:14.766 --> 00:01:18.000
Even I think that for someone like me
whose face tends to look sunken (??

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.033
My face might get cold like this.

00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:22.866
I was so scared that we just
went out to buy a beanie.

00:01:22.866 --> 00:01:26.600
The climb up this mountain range took a total of four days and three nights,
and we went with AVIDER, a Malaysian travel agency.

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:29.933
So this time,
let's leave all the paperwork to them.

00:01:29.933 --> 00:01:33.966
Because hiking here is just like in Nepal and Indonesia—you
need a local guide and a permit.

00:01:33.966 --> 00:01:36.866
Plus, we have class later,
so we don't really have time for all that traveling.

00:01:36.866 --> 00:01:39.633
It took us a little over three hours to
get here from downtown Kota Kinabalu.

00:01:39.633 --> 00:01:41.266
The place where we're staying
is really close to Da Kou.

00:01:41.266 --> 00:01:46.833
I'll go to class first, and then we'll see what kind of,
um, sparks fly on this trip.

00:01:46.833 --> 00:01:49.000
This part of Indonesia is
a little different—we're

00:01:49.333 --> 00:01:50.166
actually going hiking. OK.

00:01:50.233 --> 00:01:50.533
Dogs can't find beanies in Malaysia

00:02:06.733 --> 00:02:08.733
(it's too hot here...)

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:12.966
Finally found it XDD (in
the very corner) Tonight,

00:02:16.666 --> 00:02:18.100
I'm staying at a bed
-and-breakfast at the foot of the mountain

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:25.566
The food at this B&amp;B is absolutely
delicious! I had two

00:02:26.066 --> 00:02:27.500
servings and an extra bowl
of bitter melon noodles.

00:02:31.566 --> 00:02:34.533
300 people can participate
in the competition here.

00:02:34.533 --> 00:02:38.766
First place gets 500 yuan, which is about 4,
000 New Taiwan dollars, and then 9.8K.

00:02:38.766 --> 00:02:41.000
It looks like four peaks. I’ve just
finished filling out the form,

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:47.566
so it’s the Xitou (?? Office)
of the Sacred Mountain.

00:02:47.566 --> 00:02:51.333
This is Qunfeng, so we'll need to fill out quite a bit of information, and we still have a half
-hour class to attend.

00:02:51.333 --> 00:02:54.033
I think you should be able to
leave your bag here like this.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:01.366
A pile of paperwork (I'm going crazy)—sign up for a trail run, and you can just show up to race; it's ITRA
-certified.

00:03:04.733 --> 00:03:07.100
"No need to attend class," he said,
adding that the officials had never been there either.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:08.266
How many times have you been

00:03:08.266 --> 00:03:08.700
up there? Three times.

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:13.266
Well, then, you, you, you should explain it to them,
XDD. You're the one who has to tell them.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:22.100
I can get 6 kilograms.

00:03:22.366 --> 00:03:23.100
Let's see if there's 24 kg.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.166
You're only 7.

00:03:24.166 --> 00:03:24.900
I guessed wrong.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:26.200
Yeah, 7—that's not bad,
is it? Oh, you've gone from 24 to 7 kilograms.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:30.600
This is the one from Zpack.

00:03:30.733 --> 00:03:34.666
As for these liters—I've been wondering exactly how many liters that is.
I think it should be around 40 liters.

00:03:34.666 --> 00:03:37.033
I miss the days when I used to hike for 14 days with a 68L (oops,
I meant 62L) backpack.

00:03:38.666 --> 00:03:39.333
Let's go! Okay,

00:03:39.333 --> 00:03:45.400
we're about to arrive at the park where the trailhead is,
and we're getting ready to check in.

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:52.100
Tour Leader—Jiacheng. He’s AVIDER’s best—only the best could handle our group; otherwise,
we’d be nothing but trouble.

00:03:52.266 --> 00:03:56.966
Seeing all these peaks here—all right,
people from all over the world are gathering here now.

00:03:57.433 --> 00:03:59.000
There are so many hikers here. You
have to go with a local guide,

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:04.233
so you can't hike here on your own.

00:04:04.233 --> 00:04:09.333
This Nepal and Japan—well,
Nepal and Indonesia are the same,

00:04:09.333 --> 00:04:16.333
What’s particularly noteworthy is that guides here must be from Sabah; people from Penang,
Langkawi, Kuala Lumpur, or Malacca are not allowed.

00:04:16.333 --> 00:04:20.666
Only locals from Sabah
can join the guild.

00:04:20.666 --> 00:04:26.200
Even though we went through the travel agency AVIDER, they still required us to
use a local guide to take us up the mountain—it’s to protect the local area.

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:28.200
Business—sustainable operations,

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:40.633
right? OK. This pass, which I'll need for the next three or four days,
before I head out, before I head out.

00:04:41.066 --> 00:04:44.600
Plus, they're labeled here—there are four types of capsules,
because you can't remember them all.

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:49.566
Taurine, O2, electrolytes, RC—pretty impressive,
right? And it’s lightweight, too.

00:04:49.566 --> 00:04:50.666
Lightweight: Weighing the backpack

00:04:51.366 --> 00:04:52.800
with a large
-capacity scale

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:56.100
The trailhead looks awesome.
If TWN were to show up,

00:04:56.266 --> 00:04:58.200
that would be so cool! (Seeking Taiwanese
trail running enthusiasts!)

00:04:58.300 --> 00:04:58.666
Sure. I really

00:04:58.833 --> 00:04:59.066
want to.

00:04:59.133 --> 00:05:01.400
It's an 8K hike to the summit (the round
trip takes 3 hours and 5 minutes!).

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:02.066
Your turn. Is there anyone

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:04.000
without a TWN?

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:05.933
(Our three guides)

00:05:07.033 --> 00:05:07.600
Four seats.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:09.100
VICTORIA is the furthest. Oh dear,

00:05:09.233 --> 00:05:12.066
avoid this place.

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:12.933
Three. Those three

00:05:13.333 --> 00:05:14.533
are our guides.

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:17.133
It looks like she's
also carrying a

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:17.900
shopping basket? She
looks very chill.

00:05:18.033 --> 00:05:20.066
Okay, today we're going to
go up to that hillside hut.

00:05:20.233 --> 00:05:22.066
I gave a tutorial on
climbing 1200M in 6K,

00:05:22.266 --> 00:05:23.866
and the EP is 18.

00:05:24.066 --> 00:05:26.133
We need to get to that
location by 3 p.m.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:27.166
We hope we can make it,

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:33.566
because if we don't,
we'll be deported.

00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:35.300
Well then, we hope to
arrive today, doggy!

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:37.700
Alright, we are now officially
embarking on

00:05:38.166 --> 00:05:40.366
our ascent to the sacred
mountain range.

00:05:40.366 --> 00:05:42.533
Then most people hike the sacred mountain,
which takes two days and one night.

00:05:42.533 --> 00:05:46.100
Yes, we went on a four
-day, three-night trip, which was only opened this year.

00:05:46.466 --> 00:05:48.966
Ah, yes, sometimes that kind of itinerary does
exist; it's not a secret itinerary.

00:05:49.533 --> 00:05:51.466
However, very few people are
climbing it right now.

00:05:51.466 --> 00:05:56.300
And I learned yesterday that each group (each day) only has 12 people,
and only 12 people can go in each day.

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:58.633
So we'll basically have the entire
campsite to ourselves today.

00:05:58.966 --> 00:06:02.300
Everyone lives in a mountain
hut halfway up the mountain.

00:06:02.366 --> 00:06:03.600
So this time,

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:08.200
there are four mountains, besides the well
-known Luoshi Peak, which is over 4,000 meters high.

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:12.133
The other three are as follows: one is over 4,
000 meters high, and the other two are around 399 meters.

00:06:12.133 --> 00:06:13.900
All four of these are taller than
Jade Mountain. Alexandra,

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:17.566
Victoria, and Ah Wu XX

00:06:17.933 --> 00:06:20.766
Okay, we now have a lot,
a lot, a lot of questions.

00:06:20.766 --> 00:06:22.933
This hiking pole, this pig
-shaped hiking pole...

00:06:23.566 --> 00:06:29.466
Anyway, it's so lame, it's so lame. What kind of staff is this? It's completely useless,
it's the same as always.

00:06:30.333 --> 00:06:31.933
They're all the same, just give them to me directly... (directly tossing them to the guide,
Jia Cheng XDDD)

00:06:34.766 --> 00:06:35.833
Oh, they're running!
They're running!

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:36.800
Don't you want to join in?

00:06:37.533 --> 00:06:38.066
Awesome!!! Keep it up,

00:06:39.233 --> 00:06:41.766
break the Italian record in 3 hours!

00:06:41.766 --> 00:06:44.600
At the first rest stop,

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:47.300
the toilets were good for urinating on
the way up to the middle altitude.

00:06:58.933 --> 00:06:59.766
Wow, those eyes are so bulging! Wow,

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:03.033
is this done on the back too?

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:04.900
The wooden imperial palace
(it really looks like it,

00:07:07.766 --> 00:07:11.700
it really looks like it!),
(it looks just like an imperial palace!)

00:07:12.266 --> 00:07:13.266
Compare it to the mountains
of Taiwan.

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:14.766
(Pig: The mountains of Taiwan
are really amazing.)

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:16.000
Pitcher plant. If you
put your hand in,

00:07:16.866 --> 00:07:18.300
will it bite you off? (??
I wouldn't dare!)

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:20.500
(I'm so hungry,

00:07:20.633 --> 00:07:23.533
I'm eating an energy bar.) There are trash cans on Mount Kailash,
but you're usually asked to take your trash down the mountain yourself.

00:07:23.533 --> 00:07:26.866
But since he had a trash can,
we didn't stand on ceremony.

00:07:26.866 --> 00:07:31.133
We also pay an entrance fee, which is a perpetual cycle.
They collect user fees from us.

00:07:31.466 --> 00:07:35.333
Okay, so that's the source of the 24 kg weight
(she said she used to carry 24 kg while hiking).

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:36.700
Yes, found it, caught it.

00:07:36.866 --> 00:07:37.633
Sunscreen.

00:07:37.633 --> 00:07:40.333
This sunscreen weighs
about 150 grams.

00:07:40.333 --> 00:07:44.366
You can also apply makeup while you're in the tent,
around 1 or 2 AM.

00:07:44.366 --> 00:07:45.166
How much? You can buy

00:07:45.166 --> 00:07:46.400
these dried shrimp.

00:07:52.600 --> 00:07:53.900
Ugh, he snatched the food from

00:07:59.000 --> 00:07:59.833
my hand! What a scoundrel!

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:26.166
I'll bring my own KFC

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:29.533
for Mid
-Autumn Festival.

00:08:29.533 --> 00:08:34.900
Watermelons! They're 50 yuan each now,
but they'll go up to 100 yuan each.

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:41.800
Mount Kinabalu can have toilets,
and then I discovered something.

00:08:41.800 --> 00:08:43.466
They're really good at math! Wow,

00:08:46.666 --> 00:08:55.200
amazing! I'm so impressed! (I'm
grabbing this!) iPhone 18 zoom in!!!

00:08:55.200 --> 00:09:01.000
I was so bored,

00:09:01.066 --> 00:09:02.466
but then I realized this toilet is awesome. (I discovered something boring,
but I'm so happy, haha!)

00:09:02.566 --> 00:09:04.000
Two stretchers,

00:09:04.533 --> 00:09:06.933
two stretchers, two stretchers,
three stretchers, two stretchers.

00:09:07.266 --> 00:09:08.866
Yes, because I also write the labels.

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:13.966
One packet contains
one taurine capsule.

00:09:13.966 --> 00:09:19.033
Excuse me, (Celine suddenly pulls out the room check
-out key...)

00:09:26.033 --> 00:09:27.833
When the sacred mountain encountered
the Taiwanese,

00:09:30.333 --> 00:09:37.000
he couldn't eat the stones;
he might die if he did.

00:09:37.066 --> 00:09:43.000
A huge one is under construction to accommodate the residents. If there aren't enough rooms available,
you can stay in a 4K location.

00:09:43.366 --> 00:09:43.933
Wow! So many pitcher

00:09:43.933 --> 00:09:44.600
plants!

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:04.600
Okay, the sacred mountain consists
of steep staircases but no

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:07.833
dangerous terrain.
You're just going to take this route.

00:10:07.833 --> 00:10:10.733
The intermediate mountain forest
morphology has progressed

00:10:14.133 --> 00:10:15.500
too quickly; it's
already halfway done.

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:16.800
What should I do? I'm

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:18.166
a little worried.

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:22.000
The labor force is similar
to that in Taiwan,

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:26.033
mostly manual laborers. (Listening to "Stock
Cancer Climbing a Mountain" with Hana XD)

00:10:30.666 --> 00:10:31.300
I'm panting and very tired.
This compartment is so big,

00:10:31.533 --> 00:10:36.700
it's easy to get cramps.
I need to bring cramp cream and replenish electrolytes.

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:54.600
Constantly rambling on and on,

00:10:56.133 --> 00:10:59.966
aren't you tired? Hey,
ordinary people can't keep up...

00:11:10.733 --> 00:11:14.000
The team leader kept warning us not to
walk too fast because he said the next

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:17.433
4-6K steps were a big jump and it was
easy to get cramps (I felt okay).

00:11:19.766 --> 00:11:26.800
Warships, warships, warships and Jinmian Mountain look like this,
wow, you can see it here.

00:11:28.166 --> 00:11:30.300
There should be a view,
but it's foggy right now.

00:11:35.266 --> 00:11:36.200
5K, 3000. It's fairly easy to hike,
a gentle ascent

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:43.000
all the way up,
not steep at all (I think so, haha).

00:11:46.266 --> 00:11:48.900
The vegetation was relatively short
and the area was quite open.

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:53.900
Since we were over 3000 meters,
we urged him to walk faster because it was about to rain.

00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:59.166
Last time in Nepal, the guides were exhausted;
maybe the Malaysians can hold up (???).

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:07.200
It's really going to rain.

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:38.333
We've arrived. Nalaban 3200, 3272

00:12:38.333 --> 00:12:42.633
There's a helicopter platform here,
so it's not tiring at all; it's quite relaxing.

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:48.633
This is what a normal day's hike is like,
about 1000 meters. My watch says about 1400, 1300 or 1400 is okay.

00:12:48.633 --> 00:12:54.533
6K 1400M, that's quite steep, compared to routes like the Da
Xiao Ba (Shang 99 Mountain Villa) which are 4K steep climbs.

00:12:54.533 --> 00:12:59.933
They're all tourists, so most of them have guides with them. You're guaranteed to have a guide,
so don't worry.

00:13:00.366 --> 00:13:07.766
It's a very, very sound and safe route.
I'll be waiting for our teammates for a while.

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:19.000
Ah, basically walking

00:13:20.466 --> 00:13:21.900
in zone 1.

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:25.133
Running water~ First

00:13:27.433 --> 00:13:28.633
check point

00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:38.900
There's a Vietnamese style
here. But it's quite clean,

00:13:45.666 --> 00:13:48.133
and there are no curtains.

00:13:48.333 --> 00:13:49.100
Yes, there's no curtain.

00:13:49.966 --> 00:13:54.566
So, you shake it a little,
and the wood is quite stable.

00:13:54.733 --> 00:13:56.566
Because a metal frame would
be very unstable.

00:13:56.733 --> 00:14:02.833
So when I stayed in hostels before, I would specifically choose ones with thick wood,
curtains, and lamps.

00:14:02.833 --> 00:14:05.100
Haha, and then there's
the plug (important!).

00:14:05.100 --> 00:14:09.666
Anyway, we're in the mountains,
at an altitude of over 3250 meters, which is quite incredible.

00:14:10.033 --> 00:14:12.533
The reason he was able
to build such a large,

00:14:12.533 --> 00:14:20.166
brightly lit mountain hut is that if anyone snores,
all 18 people won't be able to sleep.

00:14:20.166 --> 00:14:24.533
Then there was a toilet outlet,

00:14:24.533 --> 00:14:32.666
and the toilet itself was very clean, so you could have a good time there. Hey,
you could take a shower, you really could (but then we found out there was no hot water).

00:14:33.466 --> 00:14:34.433
And there's a water heater.

00:14:35.066 --> 00:14:36.133
So you can actually take a shower (or even
a cold shower if you're brave enough!).

00:14:36.133 --> 00:14:40.866
This is an enzyme
-based facial cleansing powder; you can wash your entire face by simply adding water.

00:14:40.866 --> 00:14:46.000
Then use this to clean your face,
isn't that great and practical? (I was stunned.)

00:14:46.333 --> 00:14:46.966
Dry shampoo

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:52.633
is welcome!

00:14:53.033 --> 00:14:54.733
Welcome! Everyone's here!

00:14:54.733 --> 00:14:56.700
The restaurant tonight.

00:14:57.800 --> 00:15:04.966
You can order a lot of delicious food; it's a very,
very historic place.

00:15:10.100 --> 00:15:14.400
Sweaters, all kinds of snacks,

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:22.733
super big! Subscribe!!

00:15:25.566 --> 00:15:27.000
This is my first time using a 300ml titanium cup,
and it's so light and easy to use!!

00:15:35.033 --> 00:15:42.766
Who brought the book? The runner
-up in the trail running race always goes to the mountain hut to read first; that's how it is in trail races. (It was Zhou Qing!)

00:15:42.766 --> 00:15:47.700
A suspenseful dance between
mountains and

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:53.700
sea (Three Little Dinner
Announcement!!)

00:15:55.966 --> 00:16:03.166
Keep queuing,

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:09.033
pay the bill, it's super lavish!! (I'm not kidding,
everything is delicious!)

00:16:19.666 --> 00:16:22.833
They also have coffee and tea
bags. This is the best,

00:16:22.833 --> 00:16:29.366
most luxurious, and most abundant meal I've ever had
at a mountain hut during my mountain climbing adventure.

00:16:29.366 --> 00:16:33.566
There is no other way,
no other way, we must come to the sacred mountain.

00:16:33.866 --> 00:16:36.966
You don't have to climb to the top; you just have
to come to the sacred mountain and pay a fee.

00:16:38.466 --> 00:16:42.933
Fried bananas, fried bananas,
fried bananas are so weird!! Hey, can you get me one?

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:44.000
Please pick two for me XDDDD I'm so
excited! This red bean and sweet potato

00:16:44.933 --> 00:16:50.300
soup is super, super delicious! This is my third bowl,
from Taiwan.

00:16:50.733 --> 00:16:55.633
If this were open in Taiwan, I would definitely come every day.
Which herbal jelly shop wants to open this red bean sago dessert shop?

00:16:55.633 --> 00:16:59.233
And inside there's also this stewed sweet
potato that's very densely packed.

00:16:59.866 --> 00:17:00.900
Super delicious!! We've
been eating for an hour now,

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:06.566
but we've only been eating for half an hour.
Eating like this is just like A joy!

00:17:06.566 --> 00:17:12.000
(Everyone sat and ate like crazy,

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:14.900
hahaha) They ate until about 7 o'clock
and then went to sleep.

00:17:14.900 --> 00:17:20.266
The second floor is lovely; there are people helping
out by carrying mattresses and other items.

00:17:20.866 --> 00:17:24.200
Some photos that are quite memorable,
like this, are pretty cool.

00:17:32.666 --> 00:17:34.266
You can buy fur here,

00:17:34.533 --> 00:17:36.066
it'll be cold.
There are lots of postcards here.

00:17:36.966 --> 00:17:40.166
