00:38:51.133 --> 00:38:56.300
Anyway, the first thing to do is push the rope up,
and I think it shouldn't be too tight, just a little loose.

00:38:56.300 --> 00:38:59.066
Anyway, it will brake when you move backward,
and push when you move upward.

00:39:00.266 --> 00:39:01.466
Hyrox player

00:39:02.500 --> 00:39:03.233
(panting)

00:39:04.066 --> 00:39:07.166
Think of it as pulling a
sled; it looks like this,

00:39:07.166 --> 00:39:13.966
similar to pulling your own weight,
so it's not very heavy.

00:39:16.266 --> 00:39:17.266
I've convinced
you (XD). Everyone,

00:39:17.433 --> 00:39:19.466
take a look at this steepness;
this is what it looks like.

00:39:19.933 --> 00:39:21.100
What route does this resemble?
I can't quite place it,

00:39:21.266 --> 00:39:25.400
maybe it's similar to the North Second Ring Road?
But the North Second Ring Road isn't that long.

00:39:25.400 --> 00:39:29.900
The central point isn't that steep,
maybe 70 or 60 or 70 degrees.

00:39:30.666 --> 00:39:35.133
So actually, there are quite a few spots to scout,
you just keep scouting and scouting.

00:39:36.466 --> 00:39:39.033
Pull this rope,
okay, step on it, it won't be slippery.

00:39:41.500 --> 00:39:43.566
Almost there! It looks like it's

00:39:48.466 --> 00:39:51.266
already stretched for 100 meters.

00:39:51.900 --> 00:39:52.833
Only 100 meters...

00:39:53.766 --> 00:39:54.166
Oh my god, local

00:39:54.166 --> 00:39:55.366
moms!!!

00:39:57.033 --> 00:39:58.133
I'm not scared,

00:39:59.133 --> 00:40:00.200
we're almost there
(just kidding, lol).

00:40:04.666 --> 00:40:06.633
He said the hardest part was the
competition to steal a woman.

00:40:06.633 --> 00:40:10.133
He said that was the furthest away,
but this hardest part is already over.

00:40:10.133 --> 00:40:11.233
I'm telling you,

00:40:11.233 --> 00:40:13.900
head over body,
I won't turn back (that V at the end).

00:40:15.000 --> 00:40:17.833
Reaching the ridgeline,

00:40:18.533 --> 00:40:19.700
this side resembles the final section
of the main peak of Nanhu.

00:40:20.400 --> 00:40:21.900
We'll be changing
to thinner rope later.

00:40:22.000 --> 00:40:22.433
We still need to change it, hmm.

00:40:22.666 --> 00:40:24.400
The rope over there is quite thin. We
should be following the ridgeline,

00:40:24.400 --> 00:40:26.733
so we need to make sure this is done.

00:40:27.400 --> 00:40:31.966
Thumb Peak is here.

00:40:33.500 --> 00:40:36.466
The platform above is white.

00:40:47.333 --> 00:40:48.866
Victoria Peak

00:40:48.933 --> 00:40:50.500
(Thumb Peak)

00:40:50.500 --> 00:40:52.033
主峰 Low`s Peak St.

00:40:52.800 --> 00:40:54.666
John's Peak

00:40:55.233 --> 00:40:58.633
This is the most beautiful spot in Jia Cheng's
opinion because you can see the entire peak.

00:41:00.400 --> 00:41:02.100
Higher than Jade Mountain among

00:41:02.100 --> 00:41:04.566
the peaks—Alexander Peak

00:41:04.566 --> 00:41:08.366
3997.5M, 2.5M short
of 4000 meters, so

00:41:08.366 --> 00:41:09.966
it's less than
4000 meters anyway.

00:41:10.100 --> 00:41:14.166
As for this mountain, as I just mentioned,
it's because very few people have visited it.

00:41:14.166 --> 00:41:15.900
So there was no need to scout out
the various granite formations.

00:41:16.866 --> 00:41:20.466
Actually, this route is quite similar to the "Later Four Peaks,
" specifically the peaks at the back (a strange realization?).

00:41:21.433 --> 00:41:27.166
Because we just came down from that V
-shaped valley, it looked like a snow-capped mountain with an emerald pool at its foot.

00:41:27.166 --> 00:41:28.100
There was no water,

00:41:28.100 --> 00:41:31.566
so we went up Firestone Mountain
from Emerald Pool.

00:41:31.566 --> 00:41:33.500
Okay, this is also dark here.

00:41:35.400 --> 00:41:40.500
I've noticed that Malaysians are very meticulous.
3997 definitely needs a 5.

00:41:40.500 --> 00:41:43.233
I really want to build a toilet now,

00:41:43.233 --> 00:41:48.800
and that sacred mountain 4095 must be marked with
2. They care a lot about that decimal point, why?

00:41:48.800 --> 00:41:52.666
This one should be named after Alexandra,
the first person to arrive.

00:41:53.166 --> 00:41:55.233
If I go first,

00:41:55.233 --> 00:41:57.100
I'll call it CP PEAK (XD Nobody explained
why it's called Thumb).

00:41:57.500 --> 00:41:58.000
I don't know why. This is John,

00:41:58.466 --> 00:42:01.433
John climbed up first.

00:42:01.433 --> 00:42:06.866
Or perhaps when he reached the summit of the mountain,
he was drinking with John (a bunch of nonsense).

00:42:07.033 --> 00:42:10.166
Uh, follow the original route,
and make sure it's like this.

00:42:11.933 --> 00:42:15.066
Let's make sure again when we reach the next V
-valley.

00:42:15.066 --> 00:42:18.900
Actually, this knot is quite useful
when traversing difficult terrain.

00:42:18.900 --> 00:42:24.133
It needs to have a strap, a D
-ring fastened, and one more important point...

00:42:24.133 --> 00:42:27.066
They kept telling you not to put your
feet on either side of the rope.

00:42:27.066 --> 00:42:30.466
It would be easier to walk if you
were on one side or the other.

00:42:30.466 --> 00:42:33.700
I still feel that it's the same as going uphill,
just relax your body a little.

00:42:33.700 --> 00:42:36.500
This way it's easier to push; if you push too hard,
it will get stuck.

00:42:47.066 --> 00:42:48.266
V-shaped valley,

00:42:52.966 --> 00:42:55.066
OK. The toilet worker
is climbing down.

00:43:03.800 --> 00:43:06.033
Well, actually, for many of the checkpoints,
you can go down sideways.

00:43:21.933 --> 00:43:22.733
That's actually

00:43:24.233 --> 00:43:25.266
a scree slope.

00:43:29.633 --> 00:43:31.300
Make sure the scree slope is okay,

00:43:49.933 --> 00:43:51.233
then come down.

00:43:54.800 --> 00:44:00.466
It seems like I have this strap, but I can't pee. It's a bit stuck. No,
I really need to pee, I absolutely have to pee.

00:44:01.300 --> 00:44:02.200
Are your legs too short? Oh,

00:44:06.433 --> 00:44:12.100
you didn't lie back, you held on with your hands. Oh,
sit down on your bottom. It's okay, it's okay, sit back.

00:44:13.466 --> 00:44:14.733
Yes, yes, yes, let's go back for

00:44:23.600 --> 00:44:25.033
lunch first (we're starving...).

00:44:41.500 --> 00:44:46.066
Today I climbed 7.4K,

00:44:46.066 --> 00:44:49.266
1000+M, and descended 500M. They're cooking here using a huge spider
-shaped stove; in Taiwan, they usually use three.

00:44:51.033 --> 00:44:52.300
Our first meal together was
fantastic! The succulent

00:44:55.333 --> 00:44:56.566
house even had cushions for seating.

00:44:56.666 --> 00:44:59.700
(You can see the Million Mountain
view from inside the house)

00:45:00.533 --> 00:45:01.933
(And there's even a fried
egg—it's ridiculous!)

00:45:03.433 --> 00:45:06.166
Richard brought up a huge can of soda
(Irunomon's number one warrior!!).

00:45:06.933 --> 00:45:07.800
The soda was so refreshing!
(But then Richard

00:45:08.600 --> 00:45:11.866
slipped and fell outside
the campsite.)

00:45:11.866 --> 00:45:16.266
(My jacket was torn)
I slipped and fell,

00:45:16.266 --> 00:45:21.066
and I have a lot of
scrapes on my hands.

00:45:21.966 --> 00:45:25.700
Be very careful, especially at special times,
especially when you change into slippers.

00:45:25.700 --> 00:45:29.300
The feel of your regular trail running shoes is different,
so you have to be very careful when stepping on them.

00:45:29.500 --> 00:45:33.733
There are many underground rivers here again,
and the places they flow through are filled with black rocks.

00:45:33.733 --> 00:45:36.366
That place is very slippery,
and it's covered in moss.

00:45:36.866 --> 00:45:40.966
Yes, he wasn't just stepping on moss,
and he was wearing his own shoes, not slippers.

00:45:40.966 --> 00:45:43.900
You need to pay extra,

00:45:44.266 --> 00:45:45.666
extra attention to the campsite.
Another thing is what you wear.

00:45:45.800 --> 00:45:48.733
Socks and flip
-flops,

00:45:48.733 --> 00:45:55.100
like me, I wear socks and Basis, and they're even regular socks, but with flip
-flops.

00:45:55.100 --> 00:46:02.333
So it's a bit unstable, which is why I have to walk to the toilet,
and eating takes a very, very slow time.

00:46:02.333 --> 00:46:06.066
Because it can be a bit slippery,
you have to be very careful at the campsite.

00:46:06.833 --> 00:46:13.066
Okay, that's a three
-person tent, a three-person tent. It's actually quite big for two people to sleep in one tent, oh.

00:46:13.066 --> 00:46:13.733
It's raining (afternoon
thunderstorms).

00:46:14.766 --> 00:46:19.333
I'll rent this sleeping bag, a pillow, and an eggshell
(these items are already included in the AVIDER itinerary).

00:46:19.333 --> 00:46:23.000
But since I can't sleep on an eggshell, I have to bring my own inflatable sleeping mat (I put the eggshell down and then add the inflatable sleeping mat,
which will make it warmer).

00:46:25.000 --> 00:46:27.366
We need to inflate it
again here, okay?

00:46:28.266 --> 00:46:29.866
Two people slept in the three
-person tent; it was indeed very spacious.

00:46:32.033 --> 00:46:33.166
(Evening...it was quite beautiful...)

00:46:39.133 --> 00:46:42.833
Ah, it's 6 o'clock now,
because we were just fast asleep.

00:46:43.500 --> 00:46:45.900
Jinse Yipian,

00:46:46.333 --> 00:46:49.433
led by Jiacheng, guided the third group to the sacred mountain peaks.
This was our third time; what about the previous two times?

00:46:49.433 --> 00:46:51.833
No team climbed all four peaks.
The scenery was quite expansive,

00:46:51.833 --> 00:46:55.500
but it was also rather ordinary,
as this area is generally like that.

00:46:56.933 --> 00:47:00.100
There are still quite a few dark clouds;
it's already past six o'clock.

00:47:00.300 --> 00:47:04.233
Our Mount Mgo,
Mgo is quite big, a large Mgo.

00:47:04.566 --> 00:47:08.966
The thickest one in Kawas, because at that time we didn't
know what the conditions were like on the mountain.

00:47:08.966 --> 00:47:10.100
Therefore, I think it's best
to bring something thick.

00:47:10.766 --> 00:47:14.700
A STATIC OCTA vest and a long
-sleeved Ulsus Alpha.

00:47:14.700 --> 00:47:18.633
Bringing three mid
-level items is perfectly fine.

00:47:18.766 --> 00:47:21.566
Okay, because this
is 3860, therefore.

00:47:21.633 --> 00:47:23.566
.. I want to emphasize this again very,
very much.

00:47:23.566 --> 00:47:29.766
Once you hear this altitude,
you must make sure you stay warm no matter the season!

00:47:29.900 --> 00:47:32.266
As I just mentioned, this is because
there are porters collaborating here.

00:47:32.266 --> 00:47:34.466
So if you can't memorize it,
just have your helper memorize it.

00:47:34.466 --> 00:47:35.933
I think I can just bring
what I need myself.

00:47:35.933 --> 00:47:38.733
When they woke up, everyone had evolved
into Pat Pat Pat Pat Pat Beasts.

00:47:39.200 --> 00:47:41.200
It must be very cold,
believe me, we all feel very cold XD

00:47:42.333 --> 00:47:43.400
My hands get very cold.

00:47:48.300 --> 00:47:50.500
(I eat with a packet of Cherry King instant noodles.
) (Highly recommend heating them up!)

00:47:53.866 --> 00:47:56.300
(Dinner was quite plentiful.)
It was mostly chicken,

00:47:56.600 --> 00:48:00.133
with pasta and meat sauce.

00:48:04.866 --> 00:48:07.400
Take two Kin Pump 5g capsules (for

00:48:08.966 --> 00:48:11.000
better sleep) after inflation.

00:48:11.000 --> 00:48:12.833
Tryptophan helps you fall asleep,

00:48:12.966 --> 00:48:14.666
and short toothbrushes
are back in action!

00:48:20.100 --> 00:48:25.400
Okay, then I'll change into these Alpha pants.
They're very warm. I've already put on my gloves.

00:48:25.400 --> 00:48:32.833
Bring an extra pair of clean socks. Yes, wear them.
You'll need to wear these Alpha sock covers when you sleep.

00:48:32.833 --> 00:48:37.500
I slept in very, very warm clothes last night. I didn't wear socks,
just Alpha socks.

00:48:41.600 --> 00:48:42.800
Almost 3900 (Getting ready to sleep,

00:48:42.800 --> 00:48:44.833
goodnight everyone!)

00:13:38.966 --> 00:13:44.500
Or, you might stay in a very cheap backpacker hostel in Beijing,
and that's what it looks like – it's always very cramped.

00:47:04.600 --> 00:47:08.966
Kawas Poway PF1000,

00:48:16.400 --> 00:48:18.466
at an altitude of nearly 3900 meters, still offers stunning views of the city skyline at night—amazing! (Plus,
a sky full of stars.)

